+
+## TL;DR
+- `3D Slicer`, `OHIF`, and `pydicom` are the strongest open-source foundations for dental CBCT, DICOM review, and imaging workflows.
+- `Whisper`, `whisper.cpp`, and `WhisperLive` are the best open-source options for chairside dictation and clinical note drafting.
+- `PaddleOCR`, `docTR`, and `Docling` are the most practical tools for forms, scanned referrals, insurance documents, and intake packets.
+- `Ollama`, `Open WebUI`, and `AnythingLLM` are strong self-hosted building blocks for local patient FAQ bots, SOP copilots, and RAG search.
+- Pure dental-native AI repos are still a gap, so this list combines verified dental projects with adjacent tools dentists can actually deploy today.
+
+## Why This List
+Most searches for the best AI tools for dentists surface proprietary products, but many practices need auditable, self-hosted, GitHub-based software for imaging, dictation, privacy, and workflow automation. Open source matters here because dental data is sensitive, workflows differ by clinic, and long-term cost control matters. The reality in 2026 is that dentist-native GitHub repos remain limited, so this list is honest about that gap and broadens into public repositories that fit real dental use cases.
+
+## Open Source Tools
+
+### Dental Imaging and Segmentation
