+> **Description:** 3D Slicer is a full medical image computing platform rather than a narrow AI model, and that is exactly why so many dental projects build on it. The README emphasizes visualization, image computing, extensibility, and cross-platform deployment, which makes it useful for dental CBCT review, segmentation pipelines, and extension-based workflows. It is mature, heavily used in research, and flexible enough for orthodontics, oral surgery, and implant planning. GitHub lists C++ as primary, a BSD-style license, about 2,191 stars, and activity updated on 2025-11-29.
