+# Contributing
+
+Thanks for improving this awesome list.
+
+## Submission Rules
+
+- Every submission must link to a public `github.com` repository.
+- No proprietary SaaS products, closed-source services, or landing pages.
+- The repository must be relevant to dentists, dental labs, dental imaging, dental administration, or adjacent self-hosted AI workflows that a dental team can realistically use.
+- Include current GitHub metadata: stars, primary language, license, and last commit date.
+- If the tool is not dental-specific, explain the dental use case clearly.
+
+## Pull Request Checklist
+
+- Add the repo in the most relevant category.
+- Keep the description specific and based on the repository README.
+- Use the same field format as the rest of the list.
+- Verify the license from GitHub before submitting.
+- Confirm the repository is still public and actively accessible.
+
+## Rejections
+
+Submissions will be rejected if they:
+
+- Do not include a GitHub repository URL
+- Link to a product page instead of source code
+- Depend on a proprietary paid backend with no meaningful open-source repo
+- Duplicate an existing entry
+
+## Quality Standard
+
+This list prefers repositories that are actively maintained, clearly licensed, and useful in real dental workflows. If a category is thin, say so directly rather than padding the list with weak matches.
