+#### [ToothGroupNetwork](https://github.com/limhoyeon/ToothGroupNetwork)
+> **Description:** ToothGroupNetwork is a 3D dental surface segmentation repository built around the MICCAI 2022 teeth scan challenge, and the README is explicit that it includes multiple model options, preprocessing, training, and inference paths for mesh-based tooth segmentation. It is research-oriented rather than turnkey, but it is one of the more visible public repos for dental mesh labeling and classification. GitHub shows about 275 stars, Python as the primary language, an MIT license, and public activity visible through 2024, making it a useful benchmark repo for advanced users.
