+- **Stars:** 2,191 ⭐
+- **Language:** C++
+- **License:** BSD-3-Clause
+- **Last Commit:** 2025-11-29
+- **Category:** dicom, visualization
+- **Best for:** Clinics and labs that need a durable open-source platform for CBCT and 3D imaging workflows
+
+---
+
+#### [OHIF Viewers](https://github.com/OHIF/Viewers)
+> **Description:** OHIF Viewers provides a web-based imaging viewer stack for DICOM studies and is one of the strongest open-source choices for browser-based review. The README focuses on extensibility, standards support, and radiology-style workflows, but the same architecture can support dental imaging portals, second-opinion review, and multi-site image access. It is especially useful when a team wants zero local installs for image review across chairs, offices, or specialists. GitHub shows JavaScript/TypeScript as primary, MIT licensing, about 4,000 stars, and recent activity through late 2025.
