+### Local AI Assistants and Workflow Builders
+These repos matter when a dental team wants a private assistant for SOPs, treatment explanations, coding support, call scripts, or knowledge retrieval without sending everything to a hosted SaaS platform.
+
+#### [Ollama](https://github.com/ollama/ollama)
+> **Description:** Ollama makes local LLM serving straightforward, and the README is centered on pulling, running, and serving models with minimal setup friction. That makes it useful for dental offices that want private assistants for policy lookup, patient education drafts, coding prompts, or document Q&A while keeping inference on local hardware or a clinic server. It is not a full application by itself, but it is one of the easiest local model runtimes to operationalize. GitHub lists Go, an MIT license, roughly 140,000 stars, and active maintenance through late 2025.
+
