+> **Description:** Open WebUI gives a polished self-hosted chat interface for local and remote models, and the README positions it as an extensible UI for running private AI assistants. In a dental setting, that can support SOP search, treatment-plan drafting, patient education templates, or staff knowledge retrieval on top of Ollama or API-backed models. It is valuable because it reduces the need to build a custom frontend before users can test workflows. GitHub lists Python as primary, MIT licensing, and org-level repository activity updated on 2025-08-18.
