+### Documents, Intake, and OCR
+Dental practices still process scans, referrals, treatment plans, EOBs, and paper forms. These tools help convert those documents into searchable text and structured data for downstream AI workflows.
+
+#### [PaddleOCR](https://github.com/PaddlePaddle/PaddleOCR)
+> **Description:** PaddleOCR is one of the most complete open-source OCR stacks for multilingual document understanding, with models and utilities for detection, recognition, table parsing, and end-to-end document workflows. The README is broad because the project spans training, inference, and deployment, which is useful for dental groups handling forms, insurance paperwork, consent packets, and scanned referrals. It is not dental-specific, but it is one of the strongest OCR backbones available on GitHub. GitHub lists Python, Apache-2.0 licensing, roughly 55,000 stars, and active releases through late 2025.
